      "text": "## Big Picture: The Anesthesia Triad"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md#004",
      "path": [
        "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery, git-history:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md",
        "concepts": "[anesthesia, surgery]",
        "current_path": "medicine/09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:anesthesia-surgery",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[anesthesia, surgery]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "09 - Anesthesia and Perioperative Care",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│               ANESTHESIA: THREE COMPONENTS (TRIAD)                      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                         │\n│  UNCONSCIOUSNESS / HYPNOSIS                                             │\n│   Propofol, etomidate, ketamine, volatile agents (sevoflurane, etc.)   │\n│   Mechanism: GABA-A potentiation (most) or NMDA antagonism (ketamine)  │\n│                                                                         │\n│  ANALGESIA (pain control)                                               │\n│   Opioids: fentanyl, remifentanil, morphine                            │\n│   Regional: neuraxial/nerve blocks; eliminate surgical pain completely  │\n│   NSAIDs + paracetamol: multimodal analgesia; reduce opioid requirement│\n│                                                                         │\n│  MUSCLE RELAXATION                                                      │\n│   Depolarizing: succinylcholine (suxamethonium) — rapid but short-lived│\n│   Non-depolarizing: rocuronium, vecuronium, cisatracurium               │\n│   Reversal: neostigmine (anticholinesterase) or sugammadex (rocuronium) │\n│                                                                         │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │  GENERAL: all three components; intubated; mech ventilation      │   │\n│  │  REGIONAL: analgesia/motor block without unconsciousness         │   │\n│  │  LOCAL:    targeted nerve blockade; patient awake                │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
    {
