        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "09 - Anesthesia and Perioperative Care",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMECHANISM:\n  Volatile agents: halogenated ethers; \"immobilizing\" via spinal cord (not brain); hypnosis from brain\n  GABA-A potentiation (primary); NMDA antagonism; glycine modulation\n  MAC (Minimum Alveolar Concentration): alveolar concentration preventing movement in 50% subjects to incision\n    Index of potency; inversely related to oil:gas coefficient (lipid solubility)\n    Additive: 0.5 MAC volatile + 0.5 MAC N2O = 1 MAC combined"
    },
