      },
      "text": "HEPATOTOXICITY:\n  Halothane hepatitis: rare but serious; cross-sensitization with other fluorinated volatiles\n  Mechanism: oxidative biotransformation produces trifluoroacetyl (TFA) chloride → protein adducts → immune response\n  Sevoflurane/desflurane: much lower hepatotoxic potential; inorganic fluoride (nephrotoxicity only at very high doses/low-flow anesthesia)"
    },
    {
