        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "09 - Anesthesia and Perioperative Care",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nNEUROMUSCULAR JUNCTION:\n  Motor nerve releases ACh → binds nicotinic ACh receptor (nAChR) at motor end plate\n  nAChR: ligand-gated Na+/K+ channel → end plate potential → action potential → contraction\n  Depolarizing NMBAs mimic ACh; non-depolarizing NMBAs competitively block nAChR"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md#024",
      "path": [
        "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery, git-history:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md",
        "concepts": "[anesthesia, surgery]",
        "current_path": "medicine/09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:anesthesia-surgery",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[anesthesia, surgery]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "09 - Anesthesia and Perioperative Care",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SUCCINYLCHOLINE (suxamethonium) — DEPOLARIZING:\n  Structure: two ACh molecules joined; activates nAChR → initial fasciculations then paralysis\n  Phase I block: sustained depolarization → receptor desensitization → flaccid paralysis\n  Phase II block: prolonged exposure → receptor changes resemble non-depolarizing (variable)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md#025",
      "path": [
        "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery, git-history:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md",
        "concepts": "[anesthesia, surgery]",
        "current_path": "medicine/09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:anesthesia-surgery",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[anesthesia, surgery]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "09 - Anesthesia and Perioperative Care",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Duration: 5-10 minutes (pseudocholinesterase/plasma ChE hydrolyzes in plasma)\n    Pseudocholinesterase deficiency: prolonged apnea (familial; genetic variants; dibucaine number)\n  Onset: 30-60 seconds → fastest available → gold standard for RSI (rapid sequence induction)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md#026",
      "path": [
        "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery, git-history:medicine:09-anesthesia-surgery]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md",
