        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "09 - Anesthesia and Perioperative Care",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NON-DEPOLARIZING NMBAs:\n  Rocuronium: fast onset (1.2 mg/kg = RSI dose; onset 60-90 sec); intermediate duration 30-60 min\n    Benzylisoquinolinium (cisatracurium) vs aminosteroid (rocuronium, vecuronium)\n    Sugammadex (encapsulates rocuronium → rapid complete reversal within minutes — preferred over neostigmine)\n  Vecuronium: similar to rocuronium; hepatic elimination; intermediate duration\n  Cisatracurium: Hofmann degradation (non-enzymatic at physiologic pH/temperature) → organ-independent\n    Preferred in hepatic or renal failure; ICU sedation (avoid residual block)\n  Pancuronium: long-acting; renal elimination; tachycardia (vagolytic)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-ANESTHESIA-SURGERY.md#028",
