        "title": "09 - Anesthesia and Perioperative Care",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MONITORING NEUROMUSCULAR BLOCK:\n  Train-of-four (TOF): 4 supramaximal stimuli at 2 Hz; count twitches and fade\n  TOF ratio: 4th/1st twitch amplitude; ≥ 0.9 = adequate recovery for extubation\n  Post-tetanic count (PTC): deep block assessment; count twitches after 50 Hz tetanic stimulus\n```"
